    "turn_text": "Bush, no different. I mean, remember Obama sneaking over leaning over and say, let Vladimir know that after the election, I'll have more flexibility. I mean, That's way worse than Trump ever. Right. So that was Medvedevs. So you're right. So Trump did three main things, armed, armed Ukraine, tried to get them, you know, some ability to defend themselves. But remember, Obama let that slip away. So Ukraine has been in a very tough position, but Trump was willing to do that, you know, training, try to strengthen their military. But the bigger issues that he did is he what the Trump administration did is by moving forces into Poland and Romania and and the Baltics, all very critical, all things that no other president would do that Trump finally did. He finally took on NATO. And now sadly, I think we're going backwards again with Biden. I mean, this whole idea that we would keep forces from World War II astronomical prices in the UK, in Germany, in Italy, it's just mind-boggling to me the amount of money that we waste there. And it's not mission focused. It's more, you know, where do people want to live? Where do the bureaucrats want to live? Oh, my friend Merkel, we're buddies with the Germans, so we're going to go ahead and keep seven military bases there. It has nothing to do with the mission. And, you know, the mission should be for our military. What are the most strategic places around the globe that we need to be so that we can project force to keep trade lines open and to protect our allies? And that has long been a, since the fall of the Berlin Wall, it's basically been just a bloated military machine at NATO where NATO doesn't even participate. We have these huge inefficient bases that are not in strategic locations for the most part. And there's been a lack to take that on. So I would argue that what Trump did is something that should have been done 20 years ago and a lot more needs to be done. But the Biden administration, they're just gonna continue down this road of having the military go woke. Let's worry about green energy and wokeness in the military and critical race theory instead of figuring out how to win wars if we have to fight them. deter provide deterrence and stay out of politics. Unfortunately,",
