    "turn_text": "Department, we can go there too. I mean, they're completely ineffective at trying to... We just can't nation build as the bottom line. I don't even... It's impossible for us to nation build in today's environment, especially in Afghanistan. Was it a good idea that was misguided? Yeah, I think it was a good idea at the beginning. But I would say by You know, by the time we hit 2010, 2011, which you had happened there, I was around at that time, you had Obama and company who were making excuses for jihadist to pretend like Al-Qaeda was gone, remember, you know, Obama's popular deal, bin Laden's dead, Al-Qaeda's on the run. Al-Qaeda was never on the run. Al-Qaeda's always been in the web with the Taliban. We've always known that. There was never a way, all the guys who fought over there, anybody who spent a lot of time over there, you knew that country, it's just geographically challenged Afghanistan. That's why empires go there to die. Much different than Iraq, which is one of the richest countries that I've ever been to on the planet. It's rich in soil and climate and water and oil and minerals. You've got a long history in Iraq of governments working there. You don't have that in Afghanistan. And so I think sometime around that 2010, 2011, 12 timeframe, we should have changed strategies there and essentially went to a counter-terrorism only force and say, look, whenever you guys get your act together and some leaders pop up, maybe we could help you out.",
